WEBVTT

00:26.360 --> 00:30.340
Miracle Power Revenge!

00:30.570 --> 00:33.090
Shit, he's charging right at us!

00:33.350 --> 00:37.200
Brute force is the best course 
of action for them, after all.

00:37.200 --> 00:40.310
Meatheads are stupid strong 
in these situations.

00:40.690 --> 00:43.100
I should have learned 
that from Taiju, damn it!

00:44.060 --> 00:44.990
I'll handle this.

00:48.030 --> 00:52.670
Indeed, it's not for a silly deal this time.

00:53.050 --> 00:54.890
It's for a true battle.

00:55.360 --> 00:56.280
For myself.

00:57.100 --> 01:03.860
With this golden, sun-colored spear prepared 
for me by the Kingdom of Science...

01:06.530 --> 01:07.910
I will protect us!

02:39.280 --> 02:44.010
<b>Total War</b>

02:54.980 --> 02:58.130
Those hooded warriors are pretty damn strong!

02:58.130 --> 02:59.740
I told you!

02:59.740 --> 03:02.620
They were way too strong 
when we got ambushed!

03:07.490 --> 03:09.240
Too bright! I can't see!

03:09.240 --> 03:12.810
Damn it! This one's using sorcery! 
Light sorcery!

03:12.810 --> 03:15.100
It's just a mirror!

03:16.370 --> 03:19.340
All we need are bluffs. It's more than enough.

03:28.800 --> 03:30.190
<i>Ah.</i>

03:30.190 --> 03:33.310
<i>He wants to play strongman.</i>

03:39.780 --> 03:42.410
Is our Moz is being pushed back?!

03:42.410 --> 03:43.850
Because it's one on three?

03:43.850 --> 03:47.450
When has he ever been pushed 
back, even against a hundred?

03:48.650 --> 03:50.610
Kirisame-chan...

03:51.820 --> 03:53.640
Oarashi was right.

03:53.640 --> 03:57.960
These hooded intruders are quite strong.

03:59.430 --> 04:03.680
I think you should throw <i>the thing</i>.

04:07.200 --> 04:08.720
Everyone, close your eyes!

04:08.720 --> 04:11.060
The Master's power is coming!

04:15.890 --> 04:17.100
<i>That's it! Throw it!</i>

04:17.100 --> 04:18.940
<i>Throw it from there!</i>

04:20.860 --> 04:23.530
<i>Outside the petrification beam's range,</i>

04:23.530 --> 04:27.740
<i>and still enough to hit 
all the intruders at once.</i>

04:28.090 --> 04:34.420
<i>You intruders aren't idiots. I'm sure 
you're trying to stop me with sorcery.</i>

04:35.180 --> 04:38.490
<i>But you already showed me 
how it works in the cave.</i>

04:38.490 --> 04:43.420
<i>Sorcery always involves some kind of push 
or pull manipulation with your fingers.</i>

04:44.890 --> 04:46.500
<i>That's all I need to know.</i>

04:46.500 --> 04:52.000
<i>I just need to behead 
you the moment you draw.</i>

04:52.000 --> 04:55.480
<i>I already win.</i>

04:59.540 --> 05:01.330
We got her to throw the petrification device!

05:01.330 --> 05:02.570
Fly the drone!

05:02.570 --> 05:06.280
All right, we've won this!

05:22.010 --> 05:23.330
What's wrong, Ryusui?

05:23.330 --> 05:25.410
We've gotta hurry!

05:25.410 --> 05:28.340
Why'd you suddenly stop flying the drone?

05:29.400 --> 05:31.630
We've made a fatal oversight.

05:32.870 --> 05:35.310
You can always trust a sailor's instincts.

05:36.510 --> 05:37.950
Someone's got the upper hand.

05:38.310 --> 05:40.800
I can feel it in the wind!

05:42.000 --> 05:44.780
<i>Why does something feel so off?</i>

05:55.290 --> 05:58.700
I rarely see you wearing earrings.

05:58.700 --> 06:00.210
Oh, this?

06:00.210 --> 06:02.670
Not bad, right? Looks good, right?

06:03.650 --> 06:09.760
The reason I'm the most powerful is 
because even with the strongest forces,

06:09.760 --> 06:12.470
I'm still so cautious.

06:19.910 --> 06:23.190
<i>That earring on Moz...</i>

06:29.530 --> 06:30.990
<i>I knew it!</i>

06:32.760 --> 06:34.090
<i>It's the same!</i>

06:37.150 --> 06:40.500
<i>We'll all gather at the 
cliff of the howling seas.</i>

06:42.250 --> 06:44.380
Hey, hey! Hey!

06:44.380 --> 06:44.980
You!

06:44.980 --> 06:46.340
Kirisame-chan!

06:46.790 --> 06:47.750
Yes?

06:47.750 --> 06:50.650
Before you go to the intruders...

06:51.110 --> 06:57.370
Moz-chan might be in contact 
with the intruders.

06:58.180 --> 07:02.190
So test them with this.

07:03.660 --> 07:07.340
The old man wins.

07:15.210 --> 07:16.790
<i>"Feels off"?</i>

07:16.790 --> 07:18.750
<i>Science doesn't rely on gut feeling.</i>

07:18.750 --> 07:20.060
<i>Calculate fast!</i>

07:20.060 --> 07:22.040
<i>I've only got a moment to spare!</i>

07:22.850 --> 07:27.260
<i>Kirisame's toss is around 
90 km/h at 60 degrees.</i>

07:27.260 --> 07:29.710
<i>A woman's average height is 160 centimeters.</i>

07:29.710 --> 07:31.340
<i>Supposing the weapon's 200 grams</i>

07:31.340 --> 07:33.950
<i>and has a cross-sectional area 
of 20 square centimeters...</i>

07:33.950 --> 07:38.460
<i>It's got an odd shape, so let 
the drag coefficient be 0.8.</i>

07:39.890 --> 07:43.050
<i>There's no way I'm calculating that 
trajectory off the top of my head.</i>

07:43.050 --> 07:44.880
<i>The numbers aren't even firm to begin with.</i>

07:44.880 --> 07:46.410
<i>Don't get cocky!</i>

07:46.410 --> 07:48.650
<i>Minimize the variables and guesstimate!</i>

07:49.150 --> 07:51.650
<i>It'll only go up 15 meters.</i>

07:51.650 --> 07:53.960
<i>Impact area of 40 meters.</i>

07:53.960 --> 07:56.330
<i>Right in the middle of all of us?</i>

07:56.690 --> 08:00.050
<i>Which means, with this trajectory, 
wherever it goes off,</i>

08:00.050 --> 08:03.500
<i>there's no way it's going to hit just us.</i>

08:03.500 --> 08:07.590
<i>Kirisame throws with perfect precision. 
Could she have messed up? No...</i>

08:08.030 --> 08:11.170
<i>This petrification weapon was always...</i>

08:12.790 --> 08:13.980
<i>a fake!</i>

08:16.140 --> 08:18.930
Everyone, full speed! Run into the lab!

08:30.890 --> 08:31.840
<i>Moz...</i>

08:31.840 --> 08:35.320
<i>You haven't betrayed the Master, have you?</i>

08:36.870 --> 08:40.200
<i>Ibara!</i>

08:40.730 --> 08:43.220
<i>That geriatric pest!</i>

08:43.220 --> 08:46.320
<i>I guess I'll have to put 
off killing you for now.</i>

08:46.630 --> 08:50.710
<i>For now, I have to pretend not 
to be in contact with them.</i>

08:51.340 --> 08:53.310
Senku, was it?

08:53.310 --> 08:55.800
I'm coming for all of you!

08:55.800 --> 08:59.220
That was always the plan, anyway!

09:00.220 --> 09:01.220
<i>The lab?</i>

09:01.220 --> 09:03.230
<i>Why the change of plans?</i>

09:04.340 --> 09:05.640
<i>Wow...</i>

09:05.640 --> 09:09.830
<i>We've strayed completely from our 
plan, and yet no one's hesitating.</i>

09:11.930 --> 09:17.860
<i>That's their infinite trust 
in Senku... and in science.</i>

09:26.880 --> 09:27.670
Yuzuriha!

09:27.670 --> 09:28.400
Okay!

09:28.920 --> 09:30.090
Amaryllis!

09:32.730 --> 09:33.650
Ryusui!

09:39.640 --> 09:41.830
Did we get everyone?!

09:41.830 --> 09:42.690
Yeah.

09:42.690 --> 09:46.090
The lab car's fast enough to lose him.

09:46.090 --> 09:47.520
Lose him?

09:49.120 --> 09:50.440
Are you sure?

09:50.880 --> 09:52.730
When the going gets tough, 
the tough get going.

09:53.110 --> 09:55.480
Yo-kun here's got his gun,

09:55.480 --> 09:59.290
and he's gonna use it to earn a 
top position in the kingdom...

09:59.290 --> 10:04.580
I mean, this is the perfect opportunity 
to shoot Moz right where it hurts!

10:13.500 --> 10:14.480
The gun?!

10:15.580 --> 10:17.260
Why is it gone?!

10:18.200 --> 10:19.340
Wait, everyone!

10:19.340 --> 10:21.260
Magma and Gen aren't on board!

10:21.910 --> 10:26.180
Now that you mention it, 
I haven't seen them in a while!

10:26.180 --> 10:29.140
It was hard to tell with 
everyone wearing hoods.

10:32.810 --> 10:34.330
Damn it, did Magma...

10:34.330 --> 10:36.150
That bastard!

10:39.060 --> 10:41.320
Wh-Wh-Where are you going with the gun?!

10:41.320 --> 10:42.660
Magma-chan!

10:43.940 --> 10:46.330
Everyone's already gone!

10:51.910 --> 10:52.510
Huh?

10:52.510 --> 10:55.380
What are you doing out here, Magma-chan?

10:56.710 --> 10:59.420
Ouchie!

11:00.160 --> 11:04.110
Don't tell me you've forgotten my goal.

11:04.110 --> 11:06.710
I'm going to take down 
the biggest prey and claim

11:06.710 --> 11:09.060
my rightful place as head of the kingdom!

11:09.060 --> 11:12.770
To hell with all the cheap tricks!

11:12.770 --> 11:14.940
We've got this powerful weapon!

11:14.940 --> 11:17.660
Let's just go up to the enemy and shoot

11:17.660 --> 11:20.650
that old boss Ibara in the 
ass and be done with it!

11:20.650 --> 11:22.760
No, no, no!

11:22.760 --> 11:25.830
It's not that simple!

11:30.600 --> 11:31.940
Isn't that...

11:34.550 --> 11:36.330
That's our ship!

11:36.960 --> 11:47.060
Heave-ho! Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

11:51.840 --> 11:54.330
The Perseus is on the move!

11:54.330 --> 11:55.470
I see now...

11:55.470 --> 11:59.530
I was wondering why they kept it intact 
and why they were occupying it.

12:00.210 --> 12:03.450
They've been trying to 
learn how to make it move!

12:03.810 --> 12:08.990
The islanders aren't going to know 
how the machine parts work, though.

12:09.770 --> 12:11.490
They are people of the ocean.

12:11.490 --> 12:14.460
They'd have figured out the sailing 
ship components with enough time.

12:14.460 --> 12:17.210
But why is the Perseus...

12:17.210 --> 12:18.460
Walk, all of you!

12:18.700 --> 12:21.820
Get on the ship if you don't want to die!

12:28.120 --> 12:30.160
It's the people from my village!

12:30.160 --> 12:30.930
No...

12:31.840 --> 12:35.190
I suspect they're gathering everyone 
from the island onto the Perseus.

12:35.430 --> 12:38.110
Wh-Why are they doing that?

12:38.640 --> 12:43.520
That means there's nowhere 
left for us to run.

12:44.420 --> 12:48.010
It's all so simple.

12:48.010 --> 12:53.570
With everyone on the ship, 
I can check everyone.

12:53.570 --> 12:58.240
And if I don't know where 
the intruders are hiding,

12:58.240 --> 13:03.510
I can just engulf the entire island 
with the petrification beam!

13:04.030 --> 13:06.260
Sh-Shit!

13:06.500 --> 13:10.510
W-We're in huge trouble!

13:10.510 --> 13:13.000
Nah, just the opposite.

13:14.150 --> 13:16.730
When the going gets tough, 
the tough get going.

13:18.170 --> 13:21.040
We might be able to take all of it.

13:21.040 --> 13:24.820
The enemy, the kingdom, and the stone machine!

13:44.810 --> 13:46.230
Ouch!

13:50.290 --> 13:52.170
That must be Ibara.

13:52.170 --> 13:53.840
All right, I'll kill him from here!

13:53.840 --> 13:55.810
There's no way you're hitting him!

13:57.660 --> 14:00.150
<i>Why does he look so cool, though?</i>

14:00.480 --> 14:04.610
Senku, what do you mean, "take all of it"?

14:04.610 --> 14:06.140
Listen up.

14:06.140 --> 14:09.990
They did us the kindness of 
getting everyone on the ship.

14:11.650 --> 14:12.620
I see!

14:14.630 --> 14:20.040
If we show them the petrified master, 
he can't make any more excuses.

14:20.410 --> 14:24.590
All of Ibara's deeds will be revealed!

14:27.780 --> 14:30.250
The Master's position is inherited.

14:30.250 --> 14:32.100
The heir would be his child.

14:32.380 --> 14:33.660
Yeah.

14:34.400 --> 14:37.360
Which means, if Ginro's right,

14:37.950 --> 14:43.360
the rightful heir to the throne 
would be you, Soyuz.

14:50.200 --> 14:52.820
It's only people that they've 
loaded onto the ship.

14:52.820 --> 14:54.640
It doesn't look like there's any cargo.

14:55.610 --> 14:59.120
They'll likely pretend the Master has 
already boarded and leave the statue behind.

14:59.540 --> 15:01.740
They have no reason to 
take any risks moving it.

15:02.320 --> 15:06.060
Even if someone on the island 
sees the Master's statue,

15:06.060 --> 15:07.960
they'll be petrified on the spot.

15:07.960 --> 15:11.510
And that's why we're splitting 
up into two teams.

15:12.170 --> 15:15.880
The enemy's security is 
spread out hilariously thin.

15:15.880 --> 15:18.100
One team will get the Master's statue.

15:18.610 --> 15:21.750
The other team will make noise 
and buy time so they don't

15:21.750 --> 15:24.310
fumigate the whole island 
with the petrification beam.

15:25.010 --> 15:26.980
We're completely outnumbered!

15:26.980 --> 15:29.950
The gun is our only hope 
to neutralize the enemy!

15:29.950 --> 15:31.440
Damn it!

15:31.440 --> 15:33.730
I'm getting my gun back!

15:33.730 --> 15:35.950
It isn't yours, dumbass.

15:36.470 --> 15:41.830
Shit, we have to find Magma before he 
wastes all the bullets haphazardly!

15:41.830 --> 15:45.460
When has Magma been anything but haphazard?

15:45.460 --> 15:48.210
But we don't have any idea 
where to even look for him.

15:53.580 --> 15:55.850
He's there!

15:57.560 --> 15:58.810
What the?!

15:59.250 --> 16:00.730
What's wrong with this thing?

16:00.730 --> 16:02.620
It didn't even come close!

16:02.620 --> 16:05.690
Of course not! It's way too far!

16:05.690 --> 16:08.320
And we can't get any closer without a boat!

16:12.730 --> 16:15.000
It's sorcery!

16:16.220 --> 16:20.070
I used sorcery to jab a hole in the boat!

16:20.070 --> 16:24.940
Maybe I'll jab a hole in your eye next!

16:24.940 --> 16:27.300
Jab?!

16:33.250 --> 16:36.640
Now we can get a bit closer to Ibara-chan!

16:37.570 --> 16:40.630
Why am I even trying to get near him?

16:40.630 --> 16:41.780
Gen is confused!

16:41.780 --> 16:43.250
Gen getting off!

16:43.250 --> 16:44.520
Gen go home!

16:44.830 --> 16:46.270
You're a useful one.

16:46.270 --> 16:48.220
I like you.

16:48.220 --> 16:50.440
Join Mantle as my aide.

16:50.830 --> 16:52.500
What are you talking about?!

16:52.500 --> 16:55.450
An aide to the guy who killed me?!

16:59.410 --> 17:01.060
I remember that now!

17:01.060 --> 17:03.280
I totally forgot.

17:03.280 --> 17:06.670
Please try your best to remember!

17:07.320 --> 17:08.680
This is bad!

17:08.680 --> 17:13.050
Magma's already charging toward Ibara.

17:14.610 --> 17:18.280
Magma took my precious gun!

17:18.280 --> 17:21.350
We don't stand a chance if we lose it!

17:21.350 --> 17:22.420
Yeah.

17:22.420 --> 17:25.640
We're gonna have to meet 
up and fight to protect it.

17:25.910 --> 17:28.240
We'll need a boat to get close.

17:29.290 --> 17:32.200
I saw Gen stealing it with his magic tricks.

17:32.200 --> 17:33.920
What can we do, though?

17:36.200 --> 17:37.620
Why?!

17:37.620 --> 17:38.820
That's a quick solution!

17:43.860 --> 17:46.240
Literally a sinking empire!

17:58.530 --> 17:59.660
Fire!

17:59.660 --> 18:01.470
Over there! Over here!

18:01.470 --> 18:04.180
Why does it have to happen 
when there's no one here?!

18:24.100 --> 18:25.830
Are you okay, Soyuz?

18:25.830 --> 18:27.230
Oh, yeah.

18:27.640 --> 18:29.230
I-It's nothing.

18:32.880 --> 18:36.740
All right, the Master's statue is in here!

18:36.740 --> 18:38.590
Don't worry. I'll carry it!

18:41.850 --> 18:43.170
Over here!

18:43.170 --> 18:44.910
Put it out!

18:48.090 --> 18:50.760
<i>The silhouette was useful 
for tricking people.</i>

18:50.760 --> 18:53.870
<i>So I didn't want to break it, but...</i>

18:53.870 --> 18:56.040
<i>Meh. Gotta be safe.</i>

18:56.040 --> 18:59.340
<i>I don't want them to steal it, after all.</i>

18:59.340 --> 19:02.950
<i>I'll just have a sculptor make 
a similar statue later on</i>

19:02.950 --> 19:06.080
<i>and kill them so they don't talk.</i>

19:07.090 --> 19:08.280
Oh, no!

19:08.720 --> 19:10.940
I-It's over!

19:20.230 --> 19:23.320
It isn't over yet.

19:23.740 --> 19:29.140
We still have some adhesive Senku-kun 
made for us in the Kingdom of Science.

19:34.410 --> 19:36.860
You're right, Yuzuriha!

19:37.810 --> 19:40.440
<i>Some of the surfaces are discolored.</i>

19:40.440 --> 19:42.720
<i>It must have fallen apart 
and degraded over time.</i>

19:43.340 --> 19:44.860
<i>We can't revive him.</i>

20:09.290 --> 20:10.580
There, there.

20:13.210 --> 20:15.770
I could hear him crying from outside.

20:18.870 --> 20:20.290
There, there.

20:29.940 --> 20:31.070
Good boy.

20:36.170 --> 20:37.490
Soyuz.

20:47.540 --> 20:48.630
I'm sorry.

20:49.530 --> 20:50.970
I remember now.

20:52.620 --> 20:54.500
It took twenty years...

20:55.730 --> 20:57.730
but I remember everything now.

20:59.330 --> 21:00.230
Everything.

21:04.000 --> 21:05.240
Dad...

21:14.480 --> 21:19.130
I know the revival fluid 
won't bring him back anymore.

21:19.890 --> 21:24.630
But I remember exactly what he looks like.

21:25.510 --> 21:30.270
I'll fix you up with the friends I have here.

21:30.860 --> 21:33.700
Back to how you used to look!

21:36.250 --> 21:37.470
Ibara-sama!

21:38.430 --> 21:41.000
They're coming on boats!

21:45.050 --> 21:47.620
It's time for a big, fun brawl!

21:47.620 --> 21:54.120
Until the statue retrieval team arrives with 
the Master's statue, ten billion percent!

21:54.350 --> 21:55.190
Yeah!

21:55.190 --> 21:58.500
I'll trust them, and use this spear 
to make time for them!

22:00.130 --> 22:03.710
I'll take down that boss with one shot!

22:04.110 --> 22:08.080
I'll stop that idiot from 
wasting all our ammo!

23:52.030 --> 23:55.010
<b>Next Episode</b>

23:54.990 --> 24:00.000
<b>This is a work of fiction, but the plants, 
animals, and production methods described are based on reality.
Foraging and making things on your own accord is extremely dangerous
and, in some cases, illegal. Please do not imitate without expertise.</b>
